xt{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186064772 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534637 true] [17592186064772 1100 "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186064772 1100 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\cot xdx$?" 13194139534637 false] [17592186064772 1145 "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186298553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300170 13194139534637 true] [17592186300146 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300147 13194139534637 true] [17592186300146 1089 "q-114306" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300146 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534637 true] [17592186300146 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300146 1113 #uuid "90fb5794-ccc5-5bbb-84a7-0497aefc34e6" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300146 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300148 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300149 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300150 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300151 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300152 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1041 "selection" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300150 13194139534637 true] [17592186300147 1110 #uuid "6954e32c-c94f-5b26-902c-8cb55225375f" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300148 1034 "3(\\sqrt{2}-2)" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300148 1111 #uuid "ebe05d70-e334-50fa-82ab-657e120476de" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300149 1034 "\\sqrt{2}+1" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300149 1111 #uuid "d098fb97-95f7-5f86-a8aa-a83703db2038" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300150 1034 "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300150 1111 #uuid "39cc65ca-fb96-563f-811a-c0e00f5e0a7a" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300151 1034 "\\sqrt{2}-3" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300151 1111 #uuid "86cf893e-69da-553f-a4e9-4fb26df5615c" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300152 1034 "3(\\sqrt{2}+1)" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300152 1111 #uuid "187fd51c-418f-5182-a575-d02a9b2d1076" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300153 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300154 13194139534637 true] [17592186300153 1089 "q-114313" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300153 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534637 true] [17592186300153 1100 "$\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300153 1113 #uuid "8642bcc0-89fd-586c-8c7c-00d4c39709e8" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300153 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300155 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300156 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300157 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300158 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300159 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1041 "selection" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300158 13194139534637 true] [17592186300154 1110 #uuid "5ccdb9d8-a843-5e82-93e0-6e7eb65611de" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300155 1034 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300155 1111 #uuid "90c6c6df-c0db-5186-b953-2b0fb9f31ec9" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300156 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300156 1111 #uuid "c99da369-f5ac-523b-b0cc-5a3fb4bb74c7" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300157 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300157 1111 #uuid "8dbeadf8-1a95-5a05-926c-031574f13c95" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300158 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300158 1111 #uuid "d47c6437-a1fb-5960-9720-e18bbfd3d39c" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300159 1034 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300159 1111 #uuid "5bfe218a-4298-5d1a-8d4a-21bc096f7b0c" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300160 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300161 13194139534637 true] [17592186300160 1089 "q-352786" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300160 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534637 true] [17592186300160 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{3}\\,x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300160 1113 #uuid "fc1564b1-ddad-50e0-ae4c-ee2d033f736e" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300160 1145 "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{3}\\,x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}\\,x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300162 13194139534637 true] [17592186300161 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534637 true] [17592186300161 1041 "field-1" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300161 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300162 13194139534637 true] [17592186300161 1110 #uuid "527507f2-7464-5fa6-a11e-d163834e2854" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300162 1034 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300162 1111 #uuid "b1730c4a-1cab-567c-bc2c-f5931f316bd1" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300163 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300164 13194139534637 true] [17592186300163 1089 "q-352797" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300163 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534637 true] [17592186300163 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300163 1113 #uuid "75c4ab91-ebb5-5fe9-9351-221cd3ae76d8" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300163 1145 "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300165 13194139534637 true] [17592186300164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300166 13194139534637 true] [17592186300164 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534637 true] [17592186300164 1041 "field-1" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300164 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300165 13194139534637 true] [17592186300164 1110 #uuid "9bfea8b5-982e-51c7-94d0-286a2e511620" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300165 1034 "\\ln(\\frac{3}{2})" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534637 true] [17592186300165 1111 #uuid "276d12cf-e996-5357-b64d-096f04206208" 13194139534637 true] [17592186300166 1034 "0" 13194139534637 true] [17592